module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.seed_admits_an_import_beside_a_same_named_declaration

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { CeilingNotStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data seed_admits_an_import_beside_a_same_named_declaration: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "seed_admits_an_import_beside_a_same_named_declaration" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: CeilingNotStated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a module imports a name it also declares. v2.std.grammar declares the GrammarExpr variant `Optional { element: GrammarExpr }` and therefore writes std.optional.Optional fully qualified at every use; gunbc#13905 (Cardinality carriers: ListHeadResult/ListTailResult -> Optional) added `Optional` to its `import std.optional { .. }` line, binding a second, unused `Optional` in the same namespace. The v1 seed builds and runs the module; v2 resolve refuses v2.std.grammar.Optional as resolve_ambiguous_at_binding_position. The seed is the lenient side: one name with two candidates is ambiguous, so the native refusal is correct.",
    "HARM: the refusal is whole-module and travels. v2.std.grammar, v2.compiler.parse (which names v2.std.grammar.Optional qualified) and v2.compiler.grammar_reach stop resolving natively, so their declarations leave the native index. PreparedGrammar is declared in v2.compiler.parse, so in native-seven's subject v2.test.claim.parse.expression_bodied_fn_decl_parse the scrutinee `dag_prepared_grammar()` gets no derived type, and the arm `Accepted { value: prepared, .. }` reads Outcome's free formal with no instance: all eight members refused at PREPARE as infer_reason_pattern_payload_formal_uninstantiated, one stage below where they stood at the parent commit. Every seed-interpreted control and the required gate stayed green, because neither asks v2 to resolve the compiler's own modules.",
    "SPECIMEN AND ATTRIBUTION (2026-10-14): //v2/test/claim/parse/expression_bodied_fn_decl_parse:all reaches EVAL on main 20b134bc9c and refuses at PREPARE on 73a8ceacd3 (gunbc#13905 alone) and on fa8479cb7b. //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-census-scoped over the same subject, at 20b134bc9c with the census verb cherry-picked and at fa8479cb7b, differs in exactly those modules: v2.std.grammar, v2.compiler.parse and v2.compiler.grammar_reach move from an infer-stage cause to resolve_reason_ambiguous_symbol, each residual located at v2.std.grammar.Optional, and the subject itself becomes a census root.",
    "DISCRIMINATOR: the same label and census at the repair commit 871358496d (main 1f6b4107a0 plus the removal of the unused import, nothing else). The label returns to EVAL for all eight members, and the census shows v2.std.grammar, v2.compiler.parse and v2.compiler.grammar_reach back at their pre-#13905 cause (infer_reason_declaration_identity_unavailable), the resolve_reason_ambiguous_symbol group empty, and the subject no longer a root.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT AND CURRENT RUNG: mechanically preventable on the native route, whose resolver refuses the ambiguity with a located binding; the seed side is outside the wall. v1 is semantics-frozen (gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing), so the seed leniency is recorded, not patched.",
    "CEILING AND NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: structurally impossible once no module is admitted through the seed resolver alone. The capability that retires the leniency's reach is the native route resolving the modules a change touches at a gate every pull request runs -- the trigger already named by gunbc.rung_drop v2_native_route_off_the_merge_path -- so an ambiguous import refuses before merge rather than in the next native census.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
